diff --git a/reference/censhu-0212-migration.md b/reference/censhu-0212-migration.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a797e95bae91e92132726995812fcb95c6f24d48
--- /dev/null
+++ b/reference/censhu-0212-migration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Local DSH migration to v0.1.212
+
+This checkout combines upstream tag v0.1.212 (`daa082ead8a8ead60311e29ad4627bff0f569fc1`) with the existing local collaborative compaction and raw-history search extensions. It is a local installation, not an upstream release.
+
+Preserved behavior includes worker-backed SQLite FTS across original and current messages, resumable batched indexing, evidence references, A/B generation with independent review and verification, planner caching, hard-pressure override, failure receipts, and append-safe background transactions. Main-model and provider configuration remain user-owned.
+
+Upstream storage schema/time metadata, bounded reads, snapshot isolation, stable message-ID token memoization, no-op fold semantics, and restart health checks are retained. The local index consumes the independent message timestamp column; an ancestor search also includes folded-away summaries. A successful no-op does not pay for another summary or count as a new fold. Host metadata and lazy content containers retain their identities.
+
+Installed-runtime acceptance exposed a stale effective-config stamp path that re-read the summary chain without its named provider recipes after the local adapter port changed. It now resolves the agent registry plus live file recipes with the same file-first precedence as model requests; 17 config-epoch/provider regressions passed, including endpoint refresh and disabled-chain behavior.
+
+Kernel-change rationale: preserve the already installed original-history search tool descriptions. No kernel algorithm or tool schema was changed for this migration. The vendored kernel is identified as `0.0.178-censhu.1`, with exact lockfile matching. Prompt fixtures and wire golden descriptions were regenerated for that explicit description change only; behavior constants and protocol rules remain unchanged.
+
+Validation uses isolated storage and local HTTP providers, including real client overflow/control/native-tool exercises, long-history FTS comparison, schema migration and cancellation recovery. A read-only online backup of the production database was opened by the candidate and checked for unchanged original tables. Paid Claude/Terra availability is an independent boundary and is not inferred from these tests.
+
+The stable production source path and profile links are preserved during installation. Back up source changes, compiled artifacts, configuration and session storage while DSH and its proxy are stopped. Restore the source/build backup to roll back; never overwrite a database backup onto history that has received newer messages.
